/*!
\page vt_page_front Vt : Value Types
\if ( PIXAR_MFB_BUILD )
\mainpage Vt : Value Types
\endif

\section vt_overview Overview

Defines classes that provide for type abstraction (VtValue) and enhanced array types (VtArray).  The Vt library also provides functions for manipulating value types.  This library operates on the level of language data types and there are differences in the C++ and Python interfaces.

\section vt_value Type Erasure with VtValue
The VtValue class wraps type objects (float, int, bool, GfVec3d, and so on) in a type-agnostic container that includes functions for determining the content type within the container.  The VtValue class is found in the C++ API only, since Python does not have the strong type restrictions of C++.  Python to C++ type conversion is handled automatically by the system.  

\section vt_python_registry Python conversion registry

Vt_ValueFromPythonRegistry owns the shared from-Python conversion registry in
the C++ library. Its header, vt/valueFromPython.h, accepts plain callback
pointers and does not include a binding implementation. Include vt/value.h
separately when defining callbacks that return VtValue.

Boost.Python modules should include vt/boost/valueFromPythonBoost.h and link
the CMake interface target vtBoostPython. It supplies the binding requirements
and selects Vt or the configured monolithic library; it adds no compiled
library. The existing VtValueFromPython<T>() and VtValueFromPythonLValue<T>()
helpers now live in that adapter header rather than vt/valueFromPython.h.
Modules register callbacks into the one core registry, including registrations
from downstream modules; they do not link against the _vt module.

Callbacks borrow their input, execute with the GIL held, and return an empty
value on a non-match. A failed conversion sets a Python exception and returns
an empty value; the module caller must propagate that exception. The Boost
adapter translates error_already_set into this contract. Registered callback
code must remain loaded for the registry's lifetime. New registrations
invalidate cached lvalue choices and take effect on the next invocation.

This separation covers the from-Python registry. Other Vt value and buffer
helpers still use Boost.Python and the full Python API during the remaining
stages of the Vt migration.

\section vt_array Shared Arrays - VtArray
The VtArray class represents an arbitrary length homogeneous container.  In the C++ API, the constructor lets you create an array of a specified size.  The VtArray interface on the Python side is implemented as a set of typed array classes (for example, BoolArray, StringArray, Vec4dArray).
*/
